<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: British firms to create 110 jobs in North Ireland.</title>
<headline>British firms to create 110 jobs in North Ireland.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three British firms said on Wednesday that they were to invest a total of 1.3 million pounds sterling on projects which would help to create 110 new jobs in Northern Ireland.</p>
<p>The investment involves British Telecom, Abbey National building society and the insurance company Prudential.  </p>
<p>British Telecom will provide 50 jobs at its software engineering centre while Abbey National will provide 38 jobs at a telephone-banking call centre.</p>
<p>Prudential will take on 22 new staff in an enlargement of its call centre for retail payment.</p>
<p>The Industrial Development Board in Northern Ireland is to contribute 0.5 million pounds sterling towards the three projects.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 6603377</p>
</text>
